## Contract flow (live)

- A task enters development only through a ready contract:
  `specs/<task-id>/contract.yaml`, **immutable to implementers**.
- Author one via `/sdlc intake` (agent-driven), or scaffold with
  `python -m taskcontract new <task-id>` and fill by hand.
- The gate: `python -m taskcontract validate specs/<task-id>/contract.yaml --profile ready`
- CI re-validates every contract on push (`.github/workflows/sdlc.yml`).

## Gate status

| Gate | What it checks here | Status |
|---|---|---|
| G0 planning/intake | contract exists and validates `ready` | 🟢 CI backstop live; venue live once `/sdlc intake` is in use |
| G1-G10 + PL-DOC + PL-PIPE | see the kit registry | 🔴 aspirational - enforcement lands via the kit's activation program |

Registry and per-gate deep pages: {{ kit_repo }}/blob/main/docs/gates.md

## Local surfaces

- `.sdlc/config.yaml` - material, stack, kit ref, active gates
- `.sdlc/clocks.yaml` - numeric gate parameters (placeholders until calibrated)
- `.sdlc/reds.yaml` - standing-red ledger: every accepted red carries an entry
- `specs/` - the protected root (see `specs/README.md`)
